{title: Oh My Darling, Clementine}
{artist: Percy Montrose, 1884}
{key: G}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 3/4}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, kids}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In a [G]cavern, in a canyon
Excavating [D]for a mine
Dwelt a [G]miner, forty-niner
And his [D]daughter [G]Clementine

{start_of_chorus}
Oh my [G]darling, oh my darling
Oh my darling [D]Clementine
You are [G]lost and gone forever
Dreadful [D]sorry, [G]Clementine

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Light she [G]was and like a fairy
And her shoes were [D]number nine
Herring [G]boxes, without topses
Sandals [D]were for [G]Clementine

{chorus}
